{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And that which is redeemed from the Levites.</b> And if one buys a house or a city from them, it goes out in the Jubilee — that sale of a house or of a city — and returns to the Levite who sold it; and it is not held permanently like the other houses of walled cities of Israel. And this גְאֻלָּה is a term of sale. Another interpretation: since it says ״גְּאֻלַּת עוֹלָם תִּהְיֶה לַלְוִיִּם,״ one might think Scripture spoke only of an Israelite purchaser who bought a house in the cities of the Levites, but a Levite who bought from a Levite — it would be held permanently. Scripture says ״וַאֲשֶׁר יִגְאַל מִן הַלְוִיִּם״ — even one who redeems from the hand of a Levite redeems with redemption of perpetuity." "<b>And the sale of the house goes out.</b> This is another commandment: and if he did not redeem it, it goes out in the Jubilee and is not held permanently at the end of the year like the house of an Israelite." "<b>For the houses of the cities of the Levites are their possession.</b> They had no inheritance of fields and vineyards, but cities to dwell in and their open spaces; therefore they serve them in place of fields, and they have redemption like fields, so that their inheritance not be cut off from them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:26.472309390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}